    "content": "In the following exercises, sketch the graph of a function with the given properties.\n\nShock waves arise in many physical applications, ranging from supernovas to detonation waves. A graph of the density of a shock wave with respect to distance, x, is shown here. We are mainly interested in the location of the front of the shock, labeled (x)_(SF) in the diagram. Evaluate munder(lim, x\u2192(x)_(SF)()^(+))\u03c1(x). Evaluate munder(lim, x\u2192(x)_(SF)()^(\u2212))\u03c1(x). Evaluate munder(lim, x\u2192(x)_(SF))\u03c1(x). Explain the physical meanings behind your answers.",
